'''Penance Mark''' is a [[mark]] [[curse]] skill that causes hits against the marked target to summon hostile [[phantasm]]s. These phantasms can be killed by you.

This skill is granted by {{il|The Hateful Accuser}}.

==Mechanics==
Penance Mark is a [[mark]] [[curse]] that targets a single enemy, causing them to spawn normal rarity enemy phantasms, 2 by default, no more than once per second. As a mark, it shares the 1 mark limit with other mark skills, does not expire due to duration, and scales with {{c|mod|Mark Effect/Effect of your Curses}}. Modifying the curse's effect scales the number of enemy Phantasms spawned, rounded down.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3452002#40|title=Path of Exile 2 and Path of Exile: Affliction Recently Asked Questions|date=December 6, 2023|accessdate=December 6, 2023}}</ref> At 67% reduced/less curse effect or greater, no Phantasms will be spawned.

===Phantasms=== 
Spawned phantasms are regular enemies and will cast a [[physical]] [[projectile]] [[spell]] to fight you while they live. Their level and therefore their maximum [[life]] depends on the [[monster level]] of the Penance Marked monster; when spawned from a level 83 monster, phantasms will have around 20,000 life. Phantasms are immune to curses, [[knockback]], and pulling effects such as {{il|Void Sphere}}. They expire after a base 3 second [[duration]], if not killed first. 

Phantasms can be used to proc on-hit, when-hit, and on-kill effects in situations with few or no additional enemies, such as [[pinnacle boss]] encounters. Phantasms grant [[flask charge]]s and [[Vaal skill|vaal soul]]s when slain but do not drop items or leave [[corpse]]s.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3452002#37|title=Path of Exile 2 and Path of Exile: Affliction Recently Asked Questions|date=December 6, 2023|accessdate=December 6, 2023}}</ref> 

Phantasms spawn a variable distance away from the marked target, typically ~2.8 to 4m in open areas. This may complicate taking advantage of effects with a limited range, such as {{il|Melee Splash Support}}, or {{psl|Master Toxicist}}'s on-kill [[poison]]ing of nearby enemies. Phantasms can be forced to spawn slightly closer than the minimum distance of 2.8m with careful character placement in relation to a map boundary, e.g. a wall. However, standing right next to a wall will force all phantasms to always spawn directly on the opposite side of the boundary in a cone at the aforementioned range.

==Version history==
Penance Mark was originally introduced as part of [[Choir of the Damned]] notable Ascendancy passive skill, of [[Warlock of the Mists]] Ascendancy class. It was an [[Affliction league]] mechanic, and the Ascendancy class is not added to the core game after the league end.
